Lab 20: Automate VM Management with Scripts
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create and execute shell scripts to automate OpenShift Virtualization VM creation, scaling, and deletion
Implement automated VM configuration backups using shell scripting and oc CLI commands
Schedule recurring backup jobs using cron
Implement error handling and logging in VM management scripts
Verify automation results using OpenShift CLI queries and log inspection
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic knowledge of Linux command line operations
Understanding of shell scripting fundamentals (bash)
Familiarity with OpenShift Virtualization concepts (VirtualMachine and VirtualMachineInstance resources)
Knowledge of Kubernetes resources and YAML syntax
Experience with cron job scheduling
Required tools (all pre-installed in the lab environment, listed here for reference):

# Verify required CLI tools are available
oc version --client
jq --version
crontab -l || echo "no crontab yet (this is fine)"
If jq is missing on a self-managed machine, install it with:

sudo dnf install -y jq
