Subtask 2.3: Schedule Recurring Backups with Cron
# Create a wrapper script that cron will invoke
cat > scripts/scheduled-backup.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
# Wrapper script for cron-scheduled backups
cd "$HOME/vm-automation" || exit 1
./scripts/backup-vm.sh backup-test-vm vm-automation 30 >> "$HOME/vm-automation/logs/cron-backup.log" 2>&1
EOF

chmod +x scripts/scheduled-backup.sh

# Install a crontab entry that runs the backup every day at 2:00 AM
( crontab -l 2>/dev/null | grep -v scheduled-backup.sh ; \
  echo "0 2 * * * $HOME/vm-automation/scripts/scheduled-backup.sh" ) | crontab -

# Verify the cron entry was installed
crontab -l | grep scheduled-backup.sh
To validate the wrapper script works correctly without waiting for the schedule, run it manually and check its log output:

./scripts/scheduled-backup.sh
cat ~/vm-automation/logs/cron-backup.log
Deliverable: crontab -l shows a line scheduling scheduled-backup.sh at 0 2 * * *, and manually running the wrapper script produces log entries in cron-backup.log matching the same format as vm-backups.log, ending with "Backup process completed successfully for backup-test-vm."

